Title:
ETWLocksmith

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
ETWLocksmith is a Windows CLI utility that enumerates and analyzes ETW (Event Tracing for Windows) provider security permissions by reading the WMI Security registry hive. It solves the problem of quickly identifying which ETW providers are accessible to which principals (SIDs/accounts) and what operations they can perform (e.g., enabling providers, creating trace sessions). The tool supports searching providers by GUID, name, or specific ETW permission bits, and can list all providers with resolved friendly names pulled from multiple registry sources (WBEM, WINEVT publishers, Autologger, etc.). It parses Windows security descriptors/DACLs to display ACE-level allow/deny entries and human-readable permission breakdowns, and applies default ETW permissions for unregistered providers. Output can be exported to JSON/CSV for auditing and diffing across hosts. It’s useful for both Red Teams (finding overly permissive telemetry surfaces) and Blue Teams (hardening/auditing ETW provider ACLs and troubleshooting tracing access issues).

Technical Focus:
- ETW provider security model and permission bits (TRACELOG_*, WMIGUID_*)
- Windows Registry parsing (HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\WMI\Security and related keys)
- Security Descriptor / DACL / ACE parsing and SID resolution
- Provider name resolution across WMI/WBEM/WINEVT/Autologger registries
- Default vs explicitly registered ETW provider permissions
- Reporting/export (JSON/CSV) for audit workflows

Use Cases:
- Audit ETW provider ACLs to find overly permissive providers (e.g., Everyone can enable/log)
- Baseline and diff ETW permission changes across endpoints for compliance/hardening
- Troubleshoot why ETW sessions/providers fail to start due to access control
- Identify candidate providers for user-mode telemetry collection without admin (where permitted)
- Generate structured reports (CSV/JSON) for fleet-wide review

Keywords:
ETW, Event Tracing for Windows, WMI Security, registry, HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\WMI\Security, security descriptor, DACL, ACE, SID, access mask, WMIGUID_QUERY, WMIGUID_SET, TRACELOG_GUID_ENABLE, TRACELOG_CREATE_REALTIME, TRACELOG_CREATE_ONDISK, WINEVT\Publishers, Autologger, WBEM Providers, Windows permissions auditing